From 5d4309b77fedf685b8433b3cbfbfb03635c36d64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:39:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(agent-lane): derive the `_answer_shape` sidecar from the
 final Agent reply

`/agent/v1/turn` never passes through route-v2's egress, so an Agent reply
reached the UI with no `_answer_shape` (measured on the real OpenAI route
captures at staging 57f903c) and rendered as free text only.

Deterministic, provider-free read-back of the shape the Agent already writes:
headline = a one-line, one-sentence first paragraph (verbatim; a `**...**`
pair is removed only when it wraps the whole sentence); bullets = the
top-level items of the first list, markers removed, capped at 3;
detail = the whole sent text. Anything else omits the key. Validated with
the conventional lane's `AnswerShapeSchema` / `isSingleSentence`.
`assistant_text` is unchanged. Attached on the main 200 path and on the
lost-response replay path (same pure derivation over the same recorded words).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
